Me again. Now:

One time, I was reading the D&D Monstrous Manual description for iron
golems (http://www.planetadnd.com/interactive_books/mm00139.php), and I
remembered that they explicitly mentioned something about the
dissipation of the gas. I wasn't sure of the details, though. But "NH
!= D&D", as the acronym goes. Long story short, I made a patch that
makes it so that green dragon blasts leave a trail of stinking clouds
in their wake.

Considering that stinking clouds are highly underused in the current
NetHack environment, I think that this patch will make green dragons
(and iron golems) more interesting, especially considering the fact
that stinking clouds confer blindness, even to poison-resistant
players.

